  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "id": 8425,
      "content": "On Wednesday, September 3 at 7:56 a.m. ET, Falcon 9 launched 28 <a href=\"https://www.starlink.com/\" target=\"_\">Starlink</a> satellites to low-Earth orbit from Space Launch Complex 40 (SLC-40) at Cape Canaveral Space Force Station in Florida."
    },
    {
      "id": 8426,
      "content": "This was the 14th flight for the Falcon 9 first stage booster supporting this mission, which previously launched Crew-8, Polaris Dawn, CRS-31, Astranis: From One to Many, IM-2, Commercial GTO-1, and now eight Starlink missions. After stage separation, the first stage landed on the A Shortfall of Gravitas droneship, which was stationed in the Atlantic Ocean."
    }
  ]
